{
  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "autoloader-generic",
      "level": "warn",
      "places": [],
      "lines": [
        "The app ships no composer/autoload.php, so the server registers its generic loader for lib/ and looks every class up in the file system.",
        "  A composer/composer.json with config.vendor-dir \".\", config.optimize-autoloader true, a config.autoloader-suffix and autoload.psr-4 {\"OCA\\\\Forms\\\\\": \"../lib/\"} makes composer dump-autoload write composer/autoload.php with a class map; the code of the app does not change."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "autoloader-authoritative",
      "level": "warn",
      "places": [
        "composer.json: config.classmap-authoritative"
      ],
      "lines": [
        "The Composer autoloader is optimized beyond level 1. The manual allows only config.optimize-autoloader: an authoritative class map breaks the upgrade of the app, and APCu is no required extension.",
        "  composer.json: config.classmap-authoritative"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "vendor-shadows-server",
      "level": "warn",
      "places": [
        "psr/http-client 1.0.3, in 3rdparty/ of Nextcloud 30 to 31",
        "psr/http-factory 1.1.0, in 3rdparty/ of Nextcloud 30 to 31",
        "psr/http-message 1.1, in 3rdparty/ of Nextcloud 30 to 31"
      ],
      "lines": [
        "vendor/ ships 3 packages that the server ships itself in a major of Nextcloud 30 to 31. Both copies define the same classes, and the autoloader that is asked first decides which version runs.",
        "  psr/http-client 1.0.3, in 3rdparty/ of Nextcloud 30 to 31",
        "  psr/http-factory 1.1.0, in 3rdparty/ of Nextcloud 30 to 31",
        "  psr/http-message 1.1, in 3rdparty/ of Nextcloud 30 to 31"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "dev-tools-in-root",
      "level": "info",
      "places": [],
      "lines": [
        "phpunit/phpunit is in require-dev of composer.json. The manual recommends a vendor-bin/ of bamarni/composer-bin-plugin per tool, so that the dependencies of a tool cannot conflict with those of the app."
      ]
    },
